# Excludes from the Docker build context shipped to the daemon.
# Anything matched here is NOT visible inside the build, regardless of
# whether the Dockerfile would have COPY'd it. Trimming the context
# keeps the per-build upload small and stops a stray .env from
# accidentally landing in an image layer.
#
# Build context: `projects/razors-edge/` (NOT the repo root). The
# Dockerfile re-installs and re-builds inside the image, so every
# install artifact below is rebuilt and must be excluded so a stale
# host `.next` / `node_modules` never shadows the in-image build.

# Workspace install + build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache

# Local environment files — secrets. razors-edge needs NO runtime
# secrets (web-only, in-memory mock — ADR-001 / ADR-003); the only
# config is the build-time `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` ARG, set in the
# Dockerfile, not from a checked-in env file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs.
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Test + review surfaces — never executed at runtime.
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/e2e
**/.review
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
lighthouserc.json

# Raw photography originals — only the graded/ derivatives + CREDITS.md
# are referenced at runtime (the app reads `/images/graded/*` only;
# see AGENT_NOTES Phase 3). The raw `public/images/*.jpg` downloads are
# `.gitignore`d already; excluding them here keeps the context lean and
# matches what actually ships.
web/public/images/*.jpg

# Photo-grading + screenshot scripts — dev-time helpers (sharp pipeline,
# capture scripts). The graded outputs are committed under
# public/images/graded/ and ship; the scripts that produced them do not.
web/scripts

# Per-project docs — readable on GitHub, not needed in the runtime image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/PLAN.md
**/PROGRESS.md
**/DECISIONS.md
**/AGENT_NOTES.md
**/CRITIQUE-*.md
**/REVIEW-*.md
**/DEPLOY.md
docs

# The build / deploy descriptors themselves — they tell the build what
# to do; they do not belong inside the resulting image.
fly.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Git metadata — not needed at runtime, and a stray fragment of the
# repo's history in a layer is a leak surface.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
